    "q-125047": {
      "dom_id": "step-q125047",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,i+\\sqrt{xy}\\,j$ and $C$ is the line segment traversed from the point $A(1,1)$ to the point $B(4,3)?$\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=(1+3t)\\,i+(1+2t)\\,j.$*",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the line segment.\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are \n$a=i+j$ and $b=4\\,i+3\\,j.$\nSo, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t(b-a) \\\\  & =(i+j)+t[(4\\,i+3\\,j)-(i+j)] \\\\  & =(i+j)+t(3i+2\\,j) \\\\  & =(1+3t)\\,i+(1+2t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ varies from $t=0$ (at the point $A$) to $t=1$ (at the point $B$).\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=1+3t,\\,y=1+2t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,i+\\sqrt{xy}\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3t+1+2t)\\,i+\\sqrt{(1+3t)(1+2t)}\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)\\,i+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+3t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t)j \\\\  & =3\\,i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)\\,i+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,j)\\cdot (3\\,i+2\\,j) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)\\cdot 3+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+2\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+2\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
