    "q-124701": {
      "dom_id": "step-q124701",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,j$ and $C$ is the line segment traversed from the point $A(3,2)$ to the point $B(1,5)?$\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=(3-2t)\\,i+(2+3t)\\,j.$*",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the line segment.\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=3\\,i+2\\,j$ and $b=i+5\\,j.$\nSo, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t(b-a) \\\\  & =(3\\,i+2\\,j)+t[(i+5\\,j)-(3\\,i+2\\,j)] \\\\  & =(3\\,i+2\\,j)+t(-2\\,i+3\\,j) \\\\  & =(3-2t)\\,i+(2+3t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ varies from $t=0$ (at the point $A$) to $t=1$ (at the point $B$).\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3-2t,\\,y=2+3t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & ={e}^{x}\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,j \\\\  & ={e}^{3-2t}\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+3t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3-2t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+3t)j \\\\  & =-2\\,i+3\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{3-2t}\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+3t)\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\,i+3\\,j) \\\\  & ={e}^{3-2t}\\cdot (-2)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+3t)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-2{e}^{3-2t}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+3t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-2{e}^{3-2t}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+3t)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
