    "q-124706": {
      "dom_id": "step-q124706",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=x\\,i+{y}^{2}\\,j$ and $C$ is the curve ${y}^{3}=x+3$ traversed from the point $A(-3,0)$ to the point $B(5,2).$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. Making $x$ the subject of the equation, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=x+3\\,⟹\\,x={y}^{3}-3.\n$$\n\nSo, the parametrization of the curve is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =({t}^{3}-3)\\,i+t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx={t}^{3}-3,\\,y=t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =x\\,i+{y}^{2}\\,j \\\\  & =({t}^{3}-3)\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(({t}^{3}-3))i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(({t}^{3}-3)\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j)\\cdot (3{t}^{2}\\,i+j) \\\\  & =({t}^{3}-3)\\cdot 3{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3{t}^{5}-9{t}^{2}+{t}^{2} \\\\  & =3{t}^{5}-8{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{t}^{5}-8{t}^{2})\\,dt \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{t}^{6}}{2}-\\frac{8{t}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{6}}{2}-\\frac{8(2)^{3}}{3})-0 \\\\  & =32-\\frac{64}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
